  "weeklyExtras": {
    "week": 8,
    "tagline": "Week 8 News · Deep History · Player Fingerprints · Week 9 Preview",
    "kicker": "GFL Insider · Week 8 Rebuilt",
    "headline": "THE STANDINGS SAY ONE THING. EIGHT WEEKS OF EVIDENCE SAY ANOTHER.",
    "deck": "Redwood reached 7-1, Ticklesh!ts reclaimed the scoring throne, Medford landed a season-saving upset, and the league's deepest weekly archive now shows exactly which players, patterns, and schedule breaks built the race.",
    "story": [
      "Week 8 widened the gap between record and performance. Redwood Murder improved to 7-1 with a 94.24-87.06 win over Off Boys, but finished ninth on the weekly scoring slate. Turbulent Ticklesh!ts scored 127.46, led the week, and reclaimed the league lead in both total points and all-play performance. The official standings still belong to Redwood; the underlying scoring profile belongs to Ticklesh!ts.",
      "The Central delivered the week's three highest scores. Ticklesh!ts finished first, Medford MountainMen scored 121.00 to upset Simpson Sith, and Flint Tropics posted 118.08 in a loss. Flint's season remains the league's sharpest record-versus-performance contradiction: 1-7 despite ranking sixth in points and sitting exactly 44-44 in all-play through eight weeks.",
      "The new player layer explains how these teams keep getting there. Josh Allen and Kenneth Walker III have each appeared among the Ticklesh!ts' ESPN-listed Top 3 performers at least five times, while Off Boys has been even more concentrated around Jahmyr Gibbs, who has appeared six times. Simpson Sith has the clearest single-player fingerprint: Jaxon Smith-Njigba has appeared in the team's Top 3 in seven of eight weeks.",
      "Your Mom continued the league's strongest recent scoring run with 123.22 against Eskimo Brothers. The roster's weekly production has repeatedly flowed through Jaylen Warren and D'Andre Swift, each with four Top-3 appearances. Medford's late surge has a similar shape: Trevor Lawrence has appeared five times, while Ja'Marr Chase and Braelon Allen have each appeared four times.",
      "The week also carried historical weight. Simpson Sith and Redwood are managed by Danny Sattler and Collin Wilson, the two founding managers identified in the league record book as still active. Their Week 9 meeting is therefore more than a 4-4 team meeting a 7-1 team; it is another chapter between the GFL's remaining original members."
    ],
